    "description": "### Impact\r\nInformation disclosure. When a post containing a `[quote]` is cooked, Discourse compares the quoted text against the original post and marks the block with a `quote-modified` or `quote-post-not-found` CSS class. This comparison loaded the parent post by topic id and post number with no Guardian check, so the result reflected posts the quoting user cannot see.\r\n\r\nAny logged-in user could post a quote targeting an arbitrary topic id and post number, including private messages and posts in restricted categories.\r\n\r\n### Patches\r\nincoming\r\n\r\n### Workarounds\r\nnone",
